/-
# Locally finite simple groups with min-p for all p (Kourovka Notebook Problem 4.35)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.35 (O. H. Kegel): (well-known problem) is
there an infinite locally finite simple group satisfying the minimum condition for `p`-subgroups for
every prime `p`?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.PGroup
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFiniteSimpleFiniteRankKourovka1Problem23Wanted

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFiniteSimpleMinPKourovka4Problem35Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.35 (O. H.
Kegel). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700243 (`KOU-4.35`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

The minimum condition for `p`-subgroups is well-foundedness of the `p`-subgroups (`IsPGroup p`)
under inclusion. Locally finite (the subgroup generated by every finite set is finite) is
`IsLocallyFinite` of the Kourovka 1.23 entry, reused here. Simple is Mathlib's `IsSimpleGroup`.
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFiniteSimpleFiniteRankKourovka1Problem23Wanted

/-- Kourovka 4.35 (O. H. Kegel, well-known problem): there is an infinite locally finite simple
group satisfying the minimum condition on `p`-subgroups for every prime `p` (the `p`-subgroups,
ordered by inclusion, are well founded). -/
def existsInfiniteLocallyFiniteSimpleMinP : Prop :=
  ∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G), Infinite G ∧ IsSimpleGroup G ∧ IsLocallyFinite G ∧
    ∀ p : ℕ, p.Prime → WellFoundedLT {H : Subgroup G // IsPGroup p H}

/--
Resolved false: Belyaev's work on locally finite groups with Chernikov Sylow `p`-subgroups shows
that no infinite locally finite simple group satisfies the minimum condition for `p`-subgroups for
every prime `p`; the Kourovka Archive answers 4.35 "No". Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov
(eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49
(2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.35 (O. H. Kegel); resolution: V. V. Belyaev, Locally
finite groups with Chernikov Sylow p-subgroups, Algebra and Logic 20 (1981), 393-402, Kourovka
Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.35: No, https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01669128.
-/
public theorem_wanted existsInfiniteLocallyFiniteSimpleMinP_refuted :
    ¬ existsInfiniteLocallyFiniteSimpleMinP

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFiniteSimpleMinPKourovka4Problem35Wanted
